  "notes": [
    "Source: archive.org scan of Sega's 'Sega Master System II Instruction Manual' (1990, US), page 3 'Parts Identification' and page 4 'BACK VIEW OF POWER BASE'; transcribed from the page images (the OCR layer drops the slot label).",
    "media: the drawing labels the 'Cartridge Slot Cover' on the top face (marked 'CARTRIDGE INPUT'): cartridge_top.",
    "controls: the power base labels 'Pause Button' and 'Power Switch'; the back view adds 'Channel Switch CH 3 - CH 4' (no contract kind). No reset button is labelled.",
    "Envelope and mass: no maker or museum figure found.",
    "ports: page 3 'Parts Identification' plus page 4 'BACK VIEW OF POWER BASE' (transcribed from the page images), filed as the complete list. Our mappings of the maker's wording: 'Control Port 1/2' -> controller_proprietary 2 (no connector standard named; coordinator ruling 2026-11-01); 'RF Jack' -> rf_out; 'AC Adaptor Jack' -> power_in."
